Arc Testnet, 2026-10-01. The interface split that grounds script/Deploy.s.sol's run()
registry-swap probe: the identity registry answers ERC-165/ERC-721, and the validation
registry has no supportsInterface and reverts the call. RPC https://rpc.testnet.arc.io.
Re-run any line below to confirm; a true answer on the identity address and a revert on
the validation address are what the deploy-time check relies on.

=== identity registry 0x8004A818BFB912233c491871b3d84c89A494BD9e ===

$ cast call 0x8004A818BFB912233c491871b3d84c89A494BD9e "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0x01ffc9a7 --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
true
$ cast call 0x8004A818BFB912233c491871b3d84c89A494BD9e "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0x80ac58cd --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
true
$ cast call 0x8004A818BFB912233c491871b3d84c89A494BD9e "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0xffffffff --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
false

=== validation registry 0x8004Cb1BF31DAf7788923b405b754f57acEB4272 ===

$ cast call 0x8004Cb1BF31DAf7788923b405b754f57acEB4272 "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0x01ffc9a7 --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
Error: server returned an error response: error code 3: execution reverted
$ cast call 0x8004Cb1BF31DAf7788923b405b754f57acEB4272 "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0x80ac58cd --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
Error: server returned an error response: error code 3: execution reverted
$ cast call 0x8004Cb1BF31DAf7788923b405b754f57acEB4272 "supportsInterface(bytes4)(bool)" 0xffffffff --rpc-url https://rpc.testnet.arc.io
Error: server returned an error response: error code 3: execution reverted

Reading:
  0x01ffc9a7 is the ERC-165 interface id and the supportsInterface selector; 0x80ac58cd is
  ERC-721; 0xffffffff is the value a spec-correct ERC-165 must answer false. The identity
  address returns true, true, false — ERC-165 that affirmatively claims ERC-721. The
  validation address reverts all three: it exposes a bespoke getValidationStatus tuple (see
  arc-probe3.log) and no supportsInterface, so an unknown selector hits no function and no
  fallback and reverts with empty data.

  This is the discriminator the two pinned registry constants' VALUES cannot both satisfy at
  once. A swap of those two addresses survives every immutable read-back in run(), because
  each then compares a constant against itself, but it puts the validation registry in the
  identity slot where supportsInterface(0x80ac58cd) no longer answers true. run() therefore
  requires ERC-721 on the identity slot and its ABSENCE on the validation slot, and refuses
  with RegistryInterfaceMismatch otherwise. The probe is read-only (eth_call) and the check
  is grounded only for these two measured addresses, which is why it lives in run() and not
  in the arbitrary-argument runWith path.
